sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-13--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch14-13: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.12";
    dc:description "The sentence states a direction toward perfection without a variable that existing or future datasets record. Proxy series of complexity or performance exist in the literature, and using them would test a different proposition. Outcomes in which organs are lost or in which organisms merely persist are compatible with the wording, so the claim does not discriminate among biological histories.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: No dataset result would confirm or refute a tendency of all bodily and mental endowments toward perfection, because perfection names no measurable variable and any gain, loss or stasis can be redescribed as fitting the organism's own conditions.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Complexity, efficiency and fitness are alternative quantities, and adopting any one of them replaces the claim.", "Perfection has no scale on which a simpler parasite, a lost eye or an unchanged structure would count as a failure.", "Relative adaptedness changes whenever the environment changes, so a long-term approach to a fixed perfection is undefined.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.78"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.118"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-13--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of darwin1859-ch14-13 by Grok 4.7: 0.15";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.15"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-13--grok>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-13--grok--data-adequacy> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
